    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature on the `POST /api/owners` create endpoint: when no registration date is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Being on `OwnerFields`, it's accepted on input and, via the `Owner` allOf, returned on output. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes/deserializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` (same mechanism already used by `Pet.birthDate`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import. MapStruct maps it automatically by name in both directions.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the SQL schema had to carry the new column.\n\n4. **`ApplyRegistrationDate.java`** (new function) \u2014 An `Apply`-style step that mutates the built `Owner` in place, setting `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when it's null, leaving a supplied date untouched.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new `applyRegistrationDate` step between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\nThe GET path required no changes \u2014 the mapper now carries `registrationDate` through to `OwnerDto` automatically.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full suite pass.",
